# Chess Lesson file
#+Title: Checkmate on promotions
#+Description: This lessons is to illustrate promotion checks and check mates
#+Author: Daniel Pedroche
#+Language: en
#+Avatar: teachers_danioche

#+StartingPosition: "8/k1P1q3/8/8/8/1KP5/8/8 w - - 0 1"

#+Begin_teacher

When the pawn gets to the last rank, it can turn into any other piece except a king.
You almost always want to promote to a queen, the most powerful piece.

#+End_teacher

#+Begin_tips

- A fun but rare exception—promoting into a royal knight fork.

#+End_tips

#+Begin_move_list

PGN: 1. *
Teacher: You turn

PGN: 1. c8=N+ *
Teacher: 👏🏻👏🏻👏🏻👏🏻 🎉🥳🎉🥳 is a fork of the king & queen, which is better than c8=Q, which nets 8 points.
Move: a7b7

PGN: 1. c8=N+ Ka7b7 *
Teacher: Ok, let's hide

PGN: 1. c8=N+ Ka7b7 2. Nc8xe7 *
Teacher: 👏🏻👏🏻👏🏻👏🏻 With the knight fork, after 1…Kb7 2.Nxe7, white’s net point gain is 11. Well done! Let's try other example. Look carefully, avoid the stealmate!
New position: 8/4KP1k/6p1/6P1/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1

PGN: 1. f8=Q *
Teacher: Oh! no! you fail! This poition is a StealMate! Try again!
New position: 8/4KP1k/6p1/6P1/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1

PGN: 1. f8=R *
Teacher: Perfect! this is one way to win! Brilliant!

#+End_move_list

#+Begin_nok_chats

- Not exactly but you can do it! Camon!

#+End_nok_chats

